  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlantic Diving Supply is a federal vendor with $2.6B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Atlantic Diving Supply recorded 46,053 awards for the period, with an average award size of $57.2K. Atlantic Diving Supply obligations fell 56.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $2.5B to Atlantic Diving Supply in FY2026 to date. Other buying agencies include the General Services Administration with $78M, the Department of State with $21.2M, and the Department of Homeland Security with $20.8M. Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest market for Atlantic Diving Supply at $1.5B, followed by All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $750M. Historical obligations show growth through FY25 followed by the current-year total: FY21 $2.9B, FY22 $3.1B, FY23 $4.6B, FY24 $4.8B, FY25 $6B, FY26 $2.6B. This snapshot covers fiscal year to date totals and includes contract obligations unless otherwise noted for award-value tables.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Atlantic Diving Supply's biggest federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $2.5B to Atlantic Diving Supply in FY2026 to date. The General Services Administration follows with $78M. The Department of State and the Department of Homeland Security each obligated $21.2M and $20.8M respectively. Smaller agency buyers include the Department of Justice at $7.1M and the Department of Energy at $944K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which product markets account for Atlantic Diving Supply's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest market at $1.5B. All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing is the next-largest market at $750M. Additional NAICS markets of note include Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $93.4M and Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing at $37.2M. Several medical and apparel markets also appear, such as Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing at $21M and Cut and Sew Apparel Contractors at $17.1M."
      }
    ]
